# s5_graph_clear_values: drop each graph value after its last consumer.
#
# table      p_census_owner_s4 (rss 2,332,684 vs peak 2,336,656 kB, 0.17%):
#              534.5 MB  n=3   unowned torch.int64 (28996, 768)      the embedding matrix, THREE times
#              453.0 MB  n=24  unowned torch.int64 (2359296,)        768 x 3072, the FFN weight shape
#              237.5 MB  n=8   unowned torch.int64 (1, 128, 28996)
#              231.2 MB  n=49  unowned torch.int64 (589824,)         768 x 768
#              178.2 MB  n=1   unowned torch.int64 (22268928,)       28996 x 768 flat: a FOURTH embedding copy
#            top five = 70% of the peak, weights held several times (s3's activation rows (1,128,768)
#            n=172 and (1,128,3072) n=33 gone after s4).
# holder     Graph.forward's values dict (local of forward; unreachable by a gc walk, hence "unowned").
# lever      graph_clear_values_cpu drops each value after its last consumer (first category).
# evidence   s7_graph_clear_values: 2,064,884 kB with a seven-lever set sharing four levers (also
#            beaver_reveal_inplace_cpu, param_mmap_release_cpu; no encrypt_spill_cpu): mechanism and gate
#            transfer, size measured here.
# order      graph_clear_values_cpu must precede param_mmap_release_cpu (not present here).
# expected   -400 to -700 MB on 2,289,520 kB (-17% to -30%); spread < 1%.
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,graph_clear_values_cpu
